01 plan-writer done [10m 65 turns $3.41 · opus · default · 1 refused]: I've written the plan for gh-9 (the SPA on a phone). One `useNarrow()` hook over matchMedia decides what counts as narrow. Below 768px the sidebar becomes a modal drawer in ChatLayout, with ☰ on every screen, focus held inside, and an `onNavigate` close passed to each of the five places that navigate from it. The thread and member panels cover the message column while it stays mounted, and a rule that the page structure is the same at every width means a rotation doesn't rebuild the page and loses nothing. The test approach is BDD outside-in: one phone journey (pick a channel from the drawer, react and reply through "⋯", go Back to the same scroll position, check nothing scrolls sideways), with the drawer rules, the panels and crossing the breakpoint proven in Vitest through the real App and ChannelView. Six decisions are marked assumed: when a new DM closes the drawer, where ☰ sits, the drawer opening on every arrival at `/`, the member panel's resets, the channel header staying visible above a panel, and read state under a panel. Nothing builds on a 🔴 entry; D20 stays open.
